            <ArticleTitle>[Metabolic indicators (&quot;risk factors&quot;) in atherosclerotic coronary heart diseases and the ability to influence these factors by diet].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In view of current interest in the so-called &quot;risk factors&quot; of atherosclerotic cardiovascular diseases and the usefulness of preventive dietary measures, a review is given of the published data from long-term prospective studies. Opinions concerning the importance of the various lipoprotein classes as risk factors and reports of a decrease in the concentration of the allegedly &quot;protective&quot; high-density lipoproteins by consumption of polyunsaturated fatty acids are discussed. An up-to-date summary of current scientific developments relative to this problem is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
